n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1+9{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{1+9{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+9{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3u)]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3u)]_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/94ad95c4f0477ae2dd29538e6cfcbbd52cbd7eda5b1c29246c1b4967566a7341.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1+9{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3a)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306962 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306963 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306964 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306965 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306966 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1041 "selection" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306965 13194139534741 true] [17592186306961 1110 #uuid "cb0e548b-dc3c-545