db/ref 17592186045465 13194139534741 true] [17592186306986 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{6}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306986 1113 #uuid "9a5e0d15-c254-5692-98e6-7c97cecac4f4" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306986 1145 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{k})+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{6}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{z}{3})]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (0-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/a4961fa6f4f1aafeba2e8f77ed91e7d034fffd6aa249f13bb8357da11a7cea5e.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{6}{{z}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}z & =2\\cdot (0-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306988 13194139534741 true] [17592186306987 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534741 true] [17592186306987 1041 "field-1" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306987 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306988 13194139534741 true] [17592186306987 1110 #uuid "1867bb57-b126-5a2a-b6c2-2e9ac5b7dcca" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306988 1034 "\\pi" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534741 true] [17592186306988 1111 #uuid "3232797b-ccb3-53ee-8389-2759ac8471c5" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306989 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306990 13194139534741 true] [17592186306989 1089 "q-351761" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306989 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534741 true] [17592186306989 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{x}^{8}+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306989 1113 #uuid "e127f88c-db6e-5b23-8bff-fce75b5840ce" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306989 1145 "First, we substitute $u={x}^{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=4{x}^{3}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{4}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{x}^{8}+4}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\infty }^{0}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}u=-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{x}^{8}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{u}{2})]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{2})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{2})]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/7151efaca7e4356e590a437f5d50a2ab6e5646e960b7ffa82b0bbed27bb9db47.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{x}^{8}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306991 13194139534741 true] [17592186306990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306992 13194139534741 true] [17592186306990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534741 true] [17592186306990 1041 "field-1" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306991 13194139534741 true] [17592186306990 1110 #uuid "90078902-e1c0-558a-852a-5caf92a1a2ac" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306991 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534741 true] [17592186306991 1111 #uuid "296a3fb4-51ec-5bdc-b7ba-a9ca7606b93b" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306992 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" 13194139534741 true] [17592186306992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534741 true] [17592186306992 1111 #uuid "ec3a3206-63d1-50f9-b943-79af46d4f7ec" 13194139534741 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-119199" 17592186306904 "q-119199/selection" 17592186306905 "q-119199/selection/49038b61ea067d6dd93788348f33b8daf64ac00ab39a6be